    "plan": "Implement: Modify DefaultDriverService.java to persist the deleted flag by calling driverRepository.save(driverDO) after setting deleted=true",
    "design": "=== Authoritative Goal ===\nThis is the real, unmediated user request - the source of truth for what is actually required. Nothing below this section may expand it: a concrete identifier, structure, or value that appears ONLY in the Planned Implementation Strategy below (never in this section) is the Planner's own implementation choice, not a new user requirement.\nFix a bug in the existing Spring Boot driver service: `DefaultDriverService.delete(Long driverId)` (in `src/main/java/com/myapp/service/driver/DefaultDriverService.java`) marks a driver as deleted in memory via `driverDO.setDeleted(true)`, but never persists that change - it does not call `driverRepository.save(driverDO)`, so the soft-delete is silently lost and the driver still shows up as active after the method returns.\n\nFix only this method so that the deleted flag is actually persisted, by saving the driver through `driverRepository` after setting `deleted` to true.\n\nDo not change the method's signature, its `@Transactional`/`@Override` annotations, or any other method in this class. Do not modify any other file in the repository.\n\n\n=== Planned Implementation Strategy ===\nThe Planner's own chosen approach for satisfying the authoritative goal above for THIS subtask - follow it, but it may be adapted if it conflicts with the authoritative goal or with real constraints discovered while implementing it.\nModify DefaultDriverService.java to persist the deleted flag by calling driverRepository.save(driverDO) after setting deleted=true\n\nAcceptance criteria assigned to this subtask:\n- The DefaultDriverService.delete(Long driverId) method correctly persists the soft-delete flag in the database by calling driverRepository.save(driverDO)\n\nFiles this subtask should touch:\n- src/main/java/com/myapp/service/driver/DefaultDriverService.java (modify)\n\nVerification: Compile DefaultDriverService.java to ensure the modification doesn't introduce compilation errors",
